# CH17 — Wings Without Chains. Skyspine mooring: three ballast anchors, Corren steps away from the last lever.

@scene CH17_ARRIVE once
say narr | The Skyspine chain has snapped. What's left of it links two new islands - and between them hangs a mooring, groaning, holding a cargo platform full of evacuees from the cliff settlement.
say edda | You're Corren's lot. He's on the mooring lever. He's been on it all night.
say edda | His plan is to cut himself loose with the load if it slips. Take the platform down with him, drop the weight, save the rest.
say tessa | That's not a plan. That's a eulogy.
say edda | There are three ballast anchors - one on the settlement, one on the old anchor rock, one on the mooring island itself. Set all three and the mooring holds without anyone on it.
say edda | My crew can't cross the gust lanes carrying the ballast. Can you?
objective dain | Set all three ballast anchors (north-west rock, settlement, mooring island). Cross the gust lanes between gusts.
@end

@scene CH17_CREW
say pilot | Wind's the same as it ever was. Pennants lift, then the gust. You'll learn it in three crossings or you'll learn it in six.
@end

@scene CH17_EVAC
say survivor | We're waiting for the platform. Nobody's going to jump. Captain Hale said so.
@end

@scene CH17_EDDA
if flag:d06p_a1,flag:d06p_a2,flag:d06p_a3 all
say edda | Three anchors. You can't count on him counting them for you.
end
label all
say edda | All three are set. Go and talk to my brother.
@end

@scene CH17_ANCHOR1
if flag:d06p_a1 done
sfx FX010
set d06p_a1
say narr | The ballast drops into the old anchor socket with a boom that rolls across the gap. The mooring line stops shivering quite so hard.
call CH17_ANCHORS
end
label done
say narr | The north-west anchor is set.
@end

@scene CH17_ANCHOR2
if flag:d06p_a2 done
sfx FX010
set d06p_a2
say narr | The settlement anchor bites into the cliff. The evacuees cheer, then look embarrassed about cheering.
call CH17_ANCHORS
end
label done
say narr | The settlement anchor is set.
@end

@scene CH17_ANCHOR3
if flag:d06p_a3 done
sfx FX010
set d06p_a3
say narr | The mooring island anchor clamps home. The platform steadies on its line.
call CH17_ANCHORS
end
label done
say narr | The mooring anchor is set.
@end

@scene CH17_ANCHORS
if flag:d06p_a1,flag:d06p_a2,flag:d06p_a3 all
say narr | (The mooring still leans on the lever. Set the remaining anchors.)
end
label all
objective dain | All three anchors are set. Talk to Corren at the mooring lever.
@end

@scene CH17_CORREN
if flag:d06p_a1,flag:d06p_a2,flag:d06p_a3 ready
say corren | You came. Don't distract me. If this slips I've got about a second to cut.
end
label ready
say corren | The line's steady.
say oriel | Three anchors are holding it. You can let go of the lever.
say corren | If I let go and I'm wrong -
say nera | Then the anchors are wrong, and we'll all be wrong together. Step away, Corren.
wait 0.6
say narr | Corren takes his hands off the lever. One finger at a time. The mooring holds.
say narr | The platform comes across, and the evacuees walk off it onto solid rock.
say edda | I'm not putting your name on the memorial.
say corren | I didn't -
say edda | I'm putting it on the rescue roster. Tuesday shift. Don't be late.
say corren | ...Tuesday.
if party:C08 pipline
goto pipdone
label pipline
say pip | I've already forged you a very convincing shift badge. Joke. Mostly.
label pipdone
if party:C07 sableline
goto sabledone
label sableline
say sable | Rescue roster. Write your own name on it. Nobody else should.
label sabledone
join C03
chapter CH17
set skyspine_anchor
objective dain | Corren is back. Skyspine's anchor is ready for the release protocol.
call REUNION_CHECK
level_floor 29
@end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- High Aerie (post)
@scene T05P_EDDA
if ch:CH17 after
say edda | My brother's on the mooring at the broken chain, south of here. Please bring him back with his hands empty.
end
label after
if ch:CH20 q03
say edda | Tuesday shift. He was early.
end
label q03
call Q03_HOOK
@end

@scene T05P_PILOT
say pilot | Windmills now instead of the hanging engines. They turn slower. They also don't scream.
@end

@scene T05P_WIND
say worker | Every windmill has a crew name painted on its vane. That was the kid's idea.
@end

@scene T05P_KID
say child | I'm going to fly rescue baskets and come home for supper. Every day. That's the plan.
@end

@scene T05P_SHOP
say keeper | Cable court traders. Half the cables are gone, so we're 'court traders' now.
shop SHOP_T05
@end

@scene T05P_SURVIVOR
say survivor | I came down on a rescue basket last winter. The pilot's not on any wall. I want her to be.
@end

@scene T05P_INN
say elder | Returners' hall. There's always room.
inn 0
@end

@scene T05P_RETURN_WALL
if flag:q03_wall wall
say narr | A clean stretch of stone beside the memorial, waiting for something.
end
label wall
say narr | The Returners' Wall. Names of people who brought others home - pilots, basket crews, a cook who ran soup across the span in a gale. And an incident archive, open to anyone.
@end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- shared reunion bookkeeping (order-independent)
@scene REUNION_CHECK
if ch:CH17,ch:CH18,ch:CH19 all
if ch:CH17 c17
say narr | (Still missing: Corren, at the broken Skyspine chain.)
label c17
if ch:CH18 c18
say narr | (Still missing: Pip, under Veyr's registry.)
label c18
if ch:CH19 c19
say narr | (Still missing: Sable, at the Whitebone sanctuary.)
label c19
end
label all
objective dain | All eight are together again. Take the evidence to Nacre's assembly for the Ash Accord.
rumor | Nacre is gathering every town's delegates by the listening pool.
@end
